.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
.Dd October 11, 2026
.Dt DTFL_STREAM_RECLOCK 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm dtfl_stream_reclock
.Nd release records at the times of a clock stream
.Sh LIBRARY
Timely and differential dataflow library
.Pq libdtfl , \-ldtfl
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In dtfl/timely_ops.h
.Ft dtfl_stream *
.Fn dtfl_stream_reclock "dtfl_stream *data" "dtfl_stream *clock"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn dtfl_stream_reclock
buffers the records of
.Fa data
until records arrive on
.Fa clock ,
then releases them at the clock's times.
A record seen on
.Fa clock
at time
.Va c
requests that all stashed data with time less than or equal to
.Va c
be emitted at time
.Va c ,
once both inputs have advanced past
.Va c .
The two streams share the scope's time class; the clock's record
payloads are ignored, only their times matter.
.Pp
This does not guarantee that every worker sees the same clock records.
To reclock on a frontier common to all workers, broadcast the clock
first.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn dtfl_stream_reclock
returns the reclocked stream, carrying the same record type as
.Fa data .
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
/* data 0..9 at times 0..9, clock ticks at 3, 5 and 8. */
dtfl_stream *out = dtfl_stream_reclock(data, clock);
/* out carries 0,1,2,3 at time 3; 4,5 at time 5; 6,7,8 at time 8. */
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr dtfl_input_new 3 ,
.Xr dtfl 7
.Sh HISTORY
This is the C form of timely's
.Vt Reclock
trait.
It is public at the pinned release
.Pq Li timely-v0.31.0
and was removed upstream afterward (#818); the port keeps the pinned
behavior.
.Sh THREAD SAFETY
The streams and the operator belong to the thread that runs the worker
and must not be used from another thread (PLAN section 5).
